'' A TOOLCHAIN FAILURE MUST NOT EXIT 0.
''
'' The tail of Run returns EXIT_USER_ERROR when the diagnostic engine holds an error
'' and EXIT_OK otherwise. That is right for everything the diagnostics know about and
'' wrong for everything they do not: a clang that will not run, a link that failed, an
'' ICE in emission. None of the three raises a diagnostic, and the call to BuildFromIr
'' discarded its result, so all three exited 0 having written no output.
''
'' Measured 2026-09-04: a win32 link failed with every runtime symbol undefined, no
'' executable was produced, and the exit code was 0. A build script cannot tell that
'' from success, and build/package.sh's --verify was written believing it could.
''
'' The missing-clang path is the one that is deterministic on any machine -- it needs
'' no clang, no linker and no runtime archive, and it fails before any of them is
'' reached. TKO_CLANG names a file that cannot exist, so this is EXIT_NO_TOOLCHAIN (3)
'' rather than EXIT_TOOL_FAILED (5): the codes are distinct because the actions are.
'' The link-failure path is not tested here, because a test that must first succeed at
'' finding clang is a test of the machine it runs on.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TKO_CLANG=tests/driver/src/no-such-clang.exe
'' ARGS: -target win64 -o tests/driver/src/toolchain-exit-out.exe tests/source/plain.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 3
'' EXPECT-OUT: clang not found
'' EXPECT-NOT: error TKO
